DEF: \u0022the Second Philippine Republic\u0022\n PSR_democratic_ADJ: \u0022Philippine\u0022\n PSR_communism: \u0022Second Philippine People\u0027s Republic\u0022\n PSR_communism_DEF: \u0022the Second Philippine People\u0027s Republic\u0022\n PSR_communism_ADJ: \u0022Philippine\u0022\n\n HBC_fascism: \u0022Hebei-Chahar Free State\u0022\n HBC_fascism_DEF: \u0022the Hebei-Chahar Free State\u0022\n HBC_democratic: \u0022Hebei-Chahar Republic\u0022\n HBC_democratic_DEF: \u0022the Hebei-Chahar Republic\u0022\n HBC_neutrality: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC_neutrality_DEF: \u0022the Hebei-Chahar Political Council\u0022\n HBC_communism: \u0022Hebei-Chahar Soviet Republic\u0022\n HBC_communism_DEF: \u0022the Hebei-Chahar Soviet Republic\u0022\n HBC_fascism_ADJ: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC_democratic_ADJ: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC_neutrality_ADJ: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC_communism_ADJ: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC_DEF: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC_ADJ: \u0022Hebei-Chahar\u0022\n HBC_autonomy_sea_warlord_subject: \u0022Hebei-Chahar Political Council\u0022\n HBC_autonomy_sea_warlord_subject_DEF: \u0022the Hebei-Chahar Political Council\u0022\n HBC_autonomy_sea_integrated_warlord_subject: \u0022Hebei-Chahar Region\u0022\n HBC_autonomy_sea_integrated_warlord_subject_DEF: \u0022the Hebei-Chahar Region\u0022\n HBC_PRC_communism_subject: \u0022Hebei-Chahar Region\u0022\n HBC_PRC_communism_subject_DEF: \u0022the Hebei-Chahar Region\u0022\n\n SDL_GER_fascism_subject:0 \u0022Reichsgau Sudetenland\u0022\n SDL_GER_fascism_subject_DEF:0 \u0022Reichsgau Sudetenland\u0022\n SDL_CZE_democratic_subject:0 \u0022Greater Krkonose-Jesenica\u0022\n SDL_CZE_communism_subject:0 \u0022Krkonose-Jesenica Commune\u0022\n SDL_democratic:0 \u0022Free Sudetenland\u0022\n SDL_democratic_DEF:0 \u0022the Sudetenland\u0022\n SDL_fascism:0 \u0022Sudetenland German Free Corps\u0022\n SDL_fascism_DEF:0 \u0022the Sudetenland\u0022\n SDL_communism:0 \u0022Sudetenland Free Workers\u0022\n SDL_communism_DEF:0 \u0022the Sudetenland Commune\u0022\n SDL:0 \u0022Sudetenland\u0022\n SDL_DEF:0 \u0022the Sudeten\u0022\n SDL_ADJ:0 \u0022Sudeten\u0022\n SDL_democratic_subject:0 \u0022$OVERLORDADJ$ $SDL$\u0022\n SDL_democratic_subject_DEF:0 \u0022$OVERLORDADJ$ $SDL$\u0022\n SDL_neutrality_subject:0 \u0022$OVERLORDADJ$ $SDL$\u0022\n SDL_neutrality_subject_DEF:0 \u0022$OVERLORDADJ$ $SDL$\u0022\n SDL_fascism_subject:0 \u0022$OVERLORDADJ$ Protectorate of $SDL$\u0022\n SDL_fascism_subject_DEF:0 \u0022the $OVERLORDADJ$ Protectorate of $SDL$\u0022\n\n RUT:0 \u0022Carpatho-Ukraine\u0022\n RUT_ADJ:0 \u0022Carpatho-Ukrainian\u0022\n RUT_DEF:0 \u0022Carpatho-Ukraine\u0022\n\n GAL: \u0022Galicia and Lodomeria\u0022\n GAL_neutrality: \u0022Kingdom of Galicia and Lodomeria\u0022\n GAL_neutrality_DEF: \u0022the Kingdom of Galicia and Lodomeria\u0022\n GAL_fascism: \u0022State of Galicia\u0022\n GAL_fascism_DEF: \u0022the State of Galicia\u0022\n GAL_democratic: \u0022Republic of Galicia\u0022\n GAL_democratic_DEF: \u0022the Republic of Galicia\u0022\n GAL_ADJ: \u0022Galician\u0022\n",
    "localisation/country_germany_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\nGER_democratic:5 \u0022Germany republic\u0022\r\nGER_democratic_DEF:5 \u0022The Germany\u0022\r\nGER_democratic_ADJ:5 \u0022Germany citizen\u0022\r\nGER_democratic_party:0 \u0022democratic front\u0022\r\nGER_democratic_party_long:0 \u0022democratic front of germany\u0022\r\nGER_neutrality:5 \u0022german empire\u0022\r\nGER_neutrality_DEF:5 \u0022The Germany\u0022\r\nGER_neutrality_ADJ:5 \u0022Germany citizen\u0022\r\nGER_neutrality_party:0 \u0022reformist faccion\u0022\r\nGER_neutrality_party_long:0 \u0022reformist faccion of the germany\u0022\r\nGER_paternal_autocrats:5 \u0022german empire\u0022\r\nGER_paternal_autocrats_DEF:5 \u0022The german empire\u0022\r\nGER_paternal_autocrats_ADJ:5 \u0022Germany citizen\u0022\r\nGER_paternal_autocrats_party:0 \u0022military junta\u0022\r\nGER_paternal_autocrats_party_long:0 \u0022\u0022\r\n",
    "localisation/decisions-la_crisis_polaca_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\nla_crisis_polaca:0 \u0022la crisis polaca\u0022\r\nla_crisis_polaca_desc:0 \u0022fue por alla en 1919 cuando tuvimos que ceder territorios por el tratado de versalles, entre ellos territorios al este de Prusia siendo el mas insulso y insultante de todos el territorio de Danzig, sin embargo eso se acabo, despu\u00E9s de a\u00F1os por fin tenemos la oportunidad de recuperar Danzig y hasta incluso mas territorios.\u0022\r\ntrabajando_a_contra_reloj:0 \u0022trabajando a contra reloj\u0022\r\ntrabajando_a_contra_reloj_desc:0 \u0022para que esto salga bien deberemos estirar las negociaciones hasta llegar a algo concreto, de lo contrario el imperio brit\u00E1nico se hartara de nosotros y nos obligara a retactarnos \u0022\r\nestirando_las_negociasiones:0 \u0022estirando las negociasiones\u0022\r\nenfriar_las_aguas:0 \u0022enfriar las aguas\u0022\r\nenfriar_las_aguas_desc:0 \u0022es de suma importancia que logremos enfriar la crisis y hacerla ver como mucho menos importante de lo que realmente es, no importa si para ello tendremos que comprar funcionarios, mentir o simplemente bajar las hostilidades temporalmente\u0022\r\nofensiva_fronteriza_en_gdyna:0 \u0022ofensiva fronteriza en Gdyna\u0022\r\nsecure_the_baltic:0 \u0022secure the baltic\u0022 \r\nsecure_the_baltic_desc:0 \u0022The Baltic states have been a point of tension between us and the West, but looking at the political landscape, perhaps we could take control of them if we invest sufficient resources. Besides, it would certainly be a great boost to the morale and loyalty of our troops. Our current influence is [?baltic_influence] we\u0027ll need at least 100 to stage a coup.\u0022\r\nimpatient_freikorps:0 \u0022impatient freikorps\u0022 \r\nimpatient_freikorps_desc:0 \u0022The Freikorps have been dissatisfied with the results of recent years due to the government\u0027s poor handling of military expansion. However, with the new \u0022hardline\u0022 government, they hope this will change. It is crucial, however, that we manage expectations carefully, as disappointing them could have unprecedented consequences. We have a loyalty of [?freikorps_loyalty] and need 100 to pacify them.\u0022\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "localisation/events_conflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.1.t:0 \u0022nuestras tropas arrazan\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.1.d:0 \u0022a nuestras tropas les fue genial en el conflicto, al punto que nuestras tropas han logrado ocupar territorios\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.1.a:0 \u0022tres hurras por alemania!!!\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.2.t:0 \u0022nuestras tropas arrazan\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.2.d:0 \u0022\\na nuestras tropas les fue genial en el conflicto, al punto que nuestras tropas han logrado ocupar territorios\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.2.a:0 \u0022tres hurras por alemania!!!\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.3.t:0 \u0022nuestras tropas arrazan\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.3.d:0 \u0022a nuestras tropas les fue genial en el conflicto, al punto que nuestras tropas han logrado ocupar territorio\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.3.a:0 \u0022tres hurras por alemania!!!\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.4.t:0 \u0022nuestras tropas fracasan....\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.4.d:0 \u0022el ataque contra polonia a fracasado completamente y ahora no solo nos vemos de manera mas agresiva si no que tambien mas debil\u0022\r\nconflictos_fronterizos_de_polonia.4.a:0 \u0022esto es una humillacion...\u0022\r\n",
    "localisation/events_for_initial_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\nevents_for_initial.1.d:0 \u0022L\u00FCttwitz looked with disdain at the economic report for the past year. It was as mediocre as it had always been since he\u0027d taken command back in 1922. However, things seemed to be changing in recent months. After all, the conflict with Poland had finally allowed him to mobilize and make good use of our already depleted war economy, for something practical and immediate. Although he knew this was only temporary, it was also something that could offer a glimmer of hope in the abyss that had been in the country for years. \\n\\nHowever, a debate remained regarding this reactivation of the economy, since the military used it as justification for mobilizing more people to the battlefield, while others spoke of taking advantage of the situation to gradually rebuild civilian industry, keeping people employed in the factories. It was a difficult decision for him. A few years ago, he wouldn\u0027t have hesitated to simply send people to war to retake the imperial possessions. However, political reality seems to have changed him more than he initially expected, so after thinking about it for a while he said to himself\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.1.a:0 \u0022wee need more soldiers\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.1.b:0 \u0022wee need more workers\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.2.t:0 \u0022a litle aproche\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.2.d:0 \u0022King Edward paused for a moment, gazing at a photograph of the former king George V, and a thought crossed his mind, did he really have to do this? He could very well be enjoying a quiet afternoon with his wife or simply indulging in his many and varied luxuries. Yet here he was, dealing with a political crisis that, honestly, he did not care about. \\n(Wolfgang Kapp enters the room)\\n-(Edward thought for a moment before speaking)\\n\u0022Very well, thank you for asking, and thank you for coming to the meeting,\u201D Edward replied.\\n\u0022I would like to get straight to the point and address directly the issues concerning the Polish crisis and its implications.\u0022-\\n(Edward did not quite know how to respond; his life had not prepared him for decisions of this kind, and besides, he honestly did not care much about the topic.)\\n\u0022\u201CUh\u2026 yes, yes, about that matter\u2026\u201D\u0022-\u201CI remind you that our nation is fully aware of how this may appear, and we assure you that the sole objective of our nation is the restoration and respect of our national pride\u2014\u201D (Edward interrupted him,) \u201CYes, yes, yes, I know, but you know, I also wanted to take the opportunity to talk about other things, you know?\u201D (Kapp looked at him, puzzled.) \u201CWhat exactly do you mean, Mr. Edward?\u201D \u201CWell, you see, I would like to know more about this \u2018German food.\u2019 I\u2019ve heard wonders about it.\u201D Kapp stared at Edward in complete disbelief. Was this the man who would soon be monarch? After some time processing this, an idea came to mind.      \\n\\n\u201COf course, Mr. Edward. We could even offer you our finest German chefs, in exchange, of course, for a little positive feedback from us.\u201D\\nEdward simply smiled.\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.2.a:0 \u0022seems like we have a deal\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.3.t:0 \u0022the bitterness of failure\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.3.d:0 \u0022The British, due to recent events, took our proposal of \u0022brotherly reconciliation\u0022 as almost an insult, and in response, our nation has just been embargoed by the empire. This scandal will go down in the history of our government as one of the worst in all of history. God have mercy on us.\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.3.a:0 \u0022DAME IT!!!\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.5.t:0 \u0022domesticated war dogs\u0022\r\nevents_for_initial.5.d:0 \u0022The Freikorps, originally created by the SPD government back in 1919, have been one of the most influential paramilitary groups of the century. Comparisons to the Soviets and the poor Keresky government are common. One might think that after Kampp\u0027s coup, the Freikorps would simply be dissolved, but time would prove otherwise. They proved to be a loophole in the Treaty of Versailles, and even when it was revised in 1921, the terms limiting the Freikorps proved to be very lax, ultimately leading to their integration into German politics.\\n\\n However, there\u0027s something that\u0027s rarely mentioned about them, something obvious to anyone who works in areas like the military:the Freikorps were mostly made up of traumatized veterans of the First World War, frustrated and angry people who, in what seemed like the end of everything they knew, banded together to save what little remained... of a world that seemed to have abandoned them. It\u0027s to be expected that, given this context, they wouldn\u0027t be so loyal to their aristocratic officers or their Supreme Commander.\\n\\n This is why there has been a recent power struggle between the regular army and the Freikorps, which, for the moment, has been contained. However, under the increasingly unified leadership of Ernst R\u00F6hm and his increasingly populist rhetoric, he seems to be attracting more and more Freikorps, both young and old. With the arrival of our new administration, it will be quite clear that the Freikorps will not be easy to appease.\u0022 \r\nevents_for_initial.5.a:0 \u0022ein, volk ein, kaiser...\u0022",
    "localisation/events_historia_del_estado_aleman_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.1.t:0 \u0022el estado aleman\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.1.d:0 \u0022El estado aleman es una entidad que es declarada en 1920 tras el golpe de estado hecho por wolf kapp y las unidades paramilitares \u201Cfreikorps\u201D\\n\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.1.a:0 \u0022si honestamente no me interesa el lore\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.1.b:0 \u0022y como paso ese golpe de estado?\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.2.t:0 \u0022EL GOLPE DE ESTADO\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.2.d:0 \u0022la conspiraci\u00F3n inicia con la sensaci\u00F3n de escepticismo de la derecha hacia la rep\u00FAblica socialdem\u00F3crata, habido pasado por un intento de revoluci\u00F3n en alemania por los llamados \u201Cespartaquistas\u201D, siendo un intento de instaurar comunismo en la joven rep\u00FAblica, es as\u00ED que el gobierno crea las unidades paramilitares conocidas como \u201Cfreikorps\u201D hechas de veteranos de la primera guerra mundial y por j\u00F3venes anti-comunistas, estas unidades aplastaron la revuelta y matar\u00EDan a los l\u00EDderes rosa luxemburgo y \u2026. Es as\u00ED como estas unidades cobran un peso extremadamente importante para m\u00E1s tarde.\\n\\npara 1920 la derecha alemana todav\u00EDa no se sent\u00EDa ni quer\u00EDa estar c\u00F3modo con la idea de una democracia liberal sin mencionar claro el tratado de versalles que proponia cosas como reducir la fuerza del ej\u00E9rcito a 100.000 cosa que claro a la derecha molesto demasiado, es por esto que organizaron un golpe de estado que no entrar\u00EDa en vigor hasta en el 29 de febrero de 1920, esto debido a que por las estipulaciones del tratado de versalles, el ej\u00E9rcito se vio obligado a disolver una brigada de la marina y un cuerpo de voluntarios, debido a esto El 10 de marzo de 1920, el general Walther von L\u00FCttwitz exigi\u00F3 del presidente Friedrich Ebert y del ministro de Defensa Gustav Noske que se dejar\u00E1 de reducir las tropas, que se disolviese el parlamento y que se eligiese el presidente directamente por el pueblo. Ebert y Noske rechazaron estas exigencias y le dieron vacaciones forzosas a von L\u00FCttwitz. Entonces von L\u00FCttwitz decidi\u00F3 llevar a cabo un golpe de Estado.\\n\\nel 13 de marzo L\u00FCttwitz decidi\u00F3 partir con una brigada a berl\u00EDn, el ej\u00E9rcito regular se neg\u00F3 a combatir a los golpistas y como resultado Friedrich Ebert y Gustav se vieron forzados a huir, de manera que Wolfgang Kapp se nombr\u00F3 a s\u00ED mismo canciller y a von L\u00FCttwitz ministro de Defensa y comandante en jefe del ej\u00E9rcito es as\u00ED como los funcionarios de berl\u00EDn se negaron a acatar sus \u00F3rdenes y llamaron a un paro general. Sin embargo debido a los comunistas todavia resentidos por los asesinatos de Rosa Luxemburgo llamaron a no hacer el paro.\\n\\nfue de esta manera que a pesar de que el paro fue en cierta parte efectivo los llamados del partido comunista a no hacer paros dificulto mucho su efectividad. De manera que con el pasar de los dias y dias, los paros fueran poco a poco perdiendo fuerza hasta que finalmente Wolfgang Kapp pudo finalmente cimentar su control sobre berl\u00EDn y cuando el partido comunista se dio cuenta de su error fue demasiado tarde. r\u00E1pidamente Wolfgang mando a banear al partido comunista y matar a todos los de este, la mayor\u00EDa terminaria huyendo a hungria y despu\u00E9s rusia y los que no terminaron masacrados por las unidades freikorps\\n\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.2.a:0 \u0022interesante\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.t:0 \u0022primeros movimientos\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.d:0 \u0022apesar de que occidente miraba con cautela y preocupacion lo que estaba ocurriendo en eso no detendria a wolfgang de hacer movimientos, de manera que para sorpresa de muchos el se reuniria con diplomaticos de la rusia comunista para negociar un apoyo militar en la guerra conntra polonia a cambio de que alemania recuperara partes de su terriotorio perdido asi como una mantencion de la independencia de los estados balticos, apesar de que este movimiento fue muy mal visto por sectores mas radicales de su gobierno como el genenral ludendorf, sin embargo esto seria vistos con ojos de terror por parte de la entente, ya que podia significar no solamente una posible alianza entre los dos estados, sino que ademas podria significar que alemania se negara a pagar las reparaciones de guerra, cosa que facilmente podria significar una invasioon por parte de inglaterra y francia, pero apesar de esto wolfgang sorprendio a todos al aceptar gran parte de las demandas de reparaciones de guerra tambien de acpeptar el tratado de versalles, solamente pidiendo como requisito la posibilidad de negociar de manera moderada ciertas cosas. De esa manera se renegociaria el tratado de versalles, consiguiendo que el ejercito se pudiera expandir hasta 500.000 hombres, que los freikorps se mantuvieran como fuerza paramilitar legal y que las reparaciones se alivianaran un poco. claro que esto no seria bien resivido por el ala mas conservadora de su gobierno,cosa que tendria consecuencias devastadoras \u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.a:0 \u0022quiero volver atr\u00E1s\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.b:0 \u0022interesante\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.t:0 \u0022intento de golpe de estado y normalizacion\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.d:0 \u0022 a pesar de que el gobierno de wolfgang se mantuvo relativamente estable en los siguientes a\u00F1os las cosas tomarian un giro drastico en 1922 con la muerte de kamppf, esto no seria desaprovechado por ludendorf y el ala conservadora que se negaba a acpetar el gobierno de continuidad de luttwitz, de manera que en la primavera de 1923, ludendorf y su sequito intentarian hacer un contra-golpe de estado, sin embargo el resultado quedo inconcluso, ya que durante los primeros dias ludendorf no fue capas de neutralizar a los lideres del ruling goverment por lo que seguiria en esos dias seria un caos absoluto, obreros tomando las calles, peleas entre las propias freikops y casi nula comunicacion, por lo que al ver lo que estaba pasando, ludendorf decidio abandonar el golpe y tratar de evitar una guerra civil o la llegada de ideas comunistas al poder, sin embargo los metodos para socabar las protestas que ludendorf y sus unidades hicieron fueron tan extremas que se le conoce como \u00BF\u0022la masacre hamburgo\u0022 donde se dio ordenes de disparar a matar a cualquiera que protestara en las calles, ludendorf no solo no se disculpo nunca sino que dijo su famosa frase \u0022lo haria una y mil veces mas de ser necesario\u0022. Apesar de el golpe de estado haber fracasado, esto no significo la muerte del ala de linea dura, debido al respeto y aprecio que tenian los oficiales a ludendorf, luttwitz sabia que apresar o siquiera obligar al retiro a ludendorf seria un movimiento demaciado arriesgado asique se centro principalmente en contener su posible influencia politica. Aunque esto sin duda fue algo que el gobierno no deseaba tuvo tambien su lado positivo, con los radicales ya agotados politicamente, luttwitz decide aprovechar la oportunidad para hacer un tratado economico con la urss que le permitiria a alemania no solo pagar sus deudas de guerra y sacarla de la crisis sino que ademas romper su aislamiento tanto economico como diplomatico, siendo sin duda un movimiento que le daria un respiro enorme al todavia joven estado aleman\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.a:0 \u0022quiero volver atr\u00E1s\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.3.b:0 \u0022interesante\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.4.t:0 \u0022consolidacion y disputas 1925-1929\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.4.d:0 \u0022 despues de esos a\u00F1os tan turbulentos, el estado aleman porfin habia encontrado una estabilidad notable, con una economia que se recuperaba y una situacion diplomatica mucho mas estable, con una poblacion que con el pasar de los a\u00F1os parecia despolitisarse y adaptarse a la nueva era, parecia que el sue\u00F1o \u0022la alemania de soldados, intelectuales y musicos\u0022 habia vuelto, sin embargo apesar de esto, el regimen provaria tener problemas a largo plazo, apesar de haber sido mas pragmatico el regimen de luttwitz seguia invirtiendo muchos recursos y atencion en el ejercito para algun dia tomar venganza de la derrota de la gran guerra, lo que no es raro que despues de mas de 10 a\u00F1os haya desgastado la economia en gran parte, por no mencionar que el tratado con la urss apesar de ser muy positivo habia vuelto a alemania dependiente economicamente a la union sovietica, por lo que la urss sin ser tonta depues de tanto tiempo se a dado cuenta de que alemania necesita mas a ellos que ellos a alemania, por lo que ha empezado a exigir cada vez mas cosas y en mayor cantidad, cosa que se a notado en la calidad de vida, el pi\u00F1o de ludendorf a hablado que lo que se necesita hacer es bajar o inlcuso detener completamente los tratos economicos con la urss, en favor de la autarquia y el desarrollo de la industria nacional. Ademas de que en respuesta a este movimiento un nuevo hombre a cogido fuerza entre los freikorps de clase baja y media que habla de que no solamente las relaciones con la urss deben seguir sino que ademas se deben expandir todo lo posible, este hombre es Ernst R\u00F6hm, alguien que dice hablar por los freikorps populares y que el verdadero nacionalismo no es el de la aristocracia que no les podrian importar menos, sino en los trabajadores pintores soladados y campesinos que son los verdaderos alemanes, naturalmente este mismo a entrado en conflicto con ludendorf y su ala conservadora radical puesto que uno representa a los freikorps de clase baja y media mientras que el otro representa a los oficiales que buscan el la obediencia total de estos mismos. El regimen para 1936 se encuentra con una situacion francamente mediocre, luttwitz ya esta cansado de tener tanto tiempo el poder y esta planeando su retiro, pero no tiene un sucesor claro, por lo que es de esperarse que todos los posibles candidatos estan como vuiltres esperando, sera ludendorf el sucesor? sera rohm? o sera otra persona del area pragmatica que tenga capas una mente mas habierta? pues esta por verse \u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.4.a:0 \u0022quiero volver atras\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.4.b:0 \u0022POR EL REICH\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.5.t:0 \u0022the knight of reaction\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.5.d:0 \u0022Someone enters the room to tell Ludendorf, a member of the military junta, that Alfred Hugenberg is preparing a reformist candidacy, sensing that Lutwitz\u0027s regime is about to end due to his old age and the state of the nation. He enters and is surprised to hear Beethoven playing and the sound of a wine glass being poured. He sees Ludendorf in his most flamboyant and understated military uniform, stuffing himself with ribs and roast potatoes. The man is taken aback and says, \u0022Hello.\u0022 \u0022What brings you here?\u0022 Ludendorf asks in a disagreeable tone. The man begins to explain in a convoluted way, given the disgusting sight of Ludendorf eating. However, when he mentions the reformist faction\u0027s candidacy, Hugenberg falls silent and begins to speak in an arrogant manner. \\n\\\u0022So the bastard is really going to do it...\u0022 he says in a contemptuous tone. \u0022That bookworm thinks he\u0027s the best alternative for Germany, that we need \u0027change,\u0027 that our regime is unsustainable...\u0022 \u201CWell, I\u2019ll tell that hypocrite who years ago was badmouthing the republic that this is sustainable and all it takes is a firmer hand, it\u2019s that simple.\u201D At this point, the informant didn\u2019t know whether to leave (which would surely be seen as disrespectful to someone like him) or stay and listen to the speech of someone clearly stuck in the 19th century.\\n\\ \u201CThe worst part\u2026 is that they don\u2019t know how to love Germany the way I do. They only want things like \u2018the language,\u2019 \u2018the food,\u2019 \u2018brotherhood,\u2019 but I say no, the real Germany is made up of soldiers, farmers, and true intellectuals, not those pathetic social democrats or like Hugenberg himself. You really don\u2019t know how sick all this-\u201D Just as he was about to finish the sentence, he realized the messenger was gone and he was talking to himself.\u0022\r\nhistoria_del_estado_aleman.5.a:0 \u0022\u0022It seems I\u0027ll have a lot to teach them when I take power.\u0022\u0022\r\n",
    "localisation/events_la_crisis_polaca_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\nla_crisis_polaca.1.t:0 \u0022The British Empire sends us an ultimatum.\u0022\r\nla_crisis_polaca.1.d:0 \u0022The British Empire has apparently stopped being quiet and has just sent us an ultimatum, telling us that we must immediately stop all hostility towards Poland or else France and they will invade us.\u0022\r\nla_crisis_polaca.2.t:0 \u0022la historia que conmovi\u00F3 alemanes\u0022\r\nla_crisis_polaca.2.d:0 \u0022This morning a story broke about a Polish girl who described losing her parents in a border conflict with Germany. Not only that, the girl described mistreatment and humiliation of civilians in the area, the worst part being that her parents weren\u0027t even soldiers. This story has already gone viral, and it is hoped that the efforts Germany has made to improve its relations with the British will soon be undone.\u0022\r\nla_crisis_polaca.2.a:0 \u0022POLISH PROPAGANDA\u0022\r\n",
    "localisation/focustree_the-freikrops-legacy_l_english.yml": "l_english: \r\nGER_la_crisis_polaca:0 \u0022The Polish Crisis\u0022\r\nGER_la_crisis_polaca_desc:0 \u0022Since the end of the Great War, the Poles have been pulling strings and occupying essential territory. For too long, we accepted this fact, timidly bowing our heads for the protection of their French lackeys. Well, no. We will show those damned Poles that they should not meddle with the German nation.\u0022\r\nGER_poniendolos_a_prueba:0 \u0022putting them to the test\u0022\r\nGER_poniendolos_a_prueba_desc:0 \u0022The Poles have been bothering us for a long time, isn\u0027t it time someone returned the favor?\u0022\r\nGER_la_lucha_en_la_mesa:0 \u0022the fight at the table\u0022\r\nGER_la_lucha_en_la_mesa_desc:0 \u0022It is quite clear to all of us that this fight is not only about the rifle, but also about the negotiating table. It is vitally important that the French do not succeed in their attempt to draw the British into this conflict; otherwise, we will be forced to withdraw.\u0022\r\nGER_activar_a_la_industria:0 \u0022activate the industry\u0022\r\nGER_activar_a_la_industria_desc:0 \u0022Our industry has been preparing for this moment, ever since the coup, although I must say it has significantly damaged our economy. Now is the time for the Prussian eagle to spread its wings.\u0022\r\nGER_quehacerconlapoblacion:0 \u0022what to do with the population?\u0022\r\nGER_quehacerconlapoblacion_desc:0 \u0022The population has been in a rather precarious situation since the 1929 crisis and\u2026 well, almost throughout our entire administration. Although with the recent revitalization of our economy, the population\u0027s situation has generally improved, at least noticeably. Now the question remains, do we focus on industry or on having more soldiers?\u0022\r\nGER_escucharalostecnocratas:0 \u0022listen to the tecnocrats?\u0022\r\nGER_escucharalostecnocratas_desc:0 \u0022Lately, a segment of the population has advocated for more pragmatic policies that move away from our vengeful efforts; however, given the precarious state of our economy, listening to technocrats could be an interesting option.\u0022\r\nGER_la_economia_es_un_juego_tramposo:0 \u0022the economy is a triki game\u0022\r\nGER_la_economia_es_un_juego_tramposo_desc:0 \u0022We tried, okay? But the situation is simply overwhelming us. The economy has been stagnant and at risk of collapse for years, and there seems to be nothing that can save it. We naively hoped that an activation against Poland might save it, but it seems that wasn\u0027t the case. For now, all we can do is pray that perhaps God will hear our pleas and that the economy can one day rise like a phoenix, but until then, all we can do is beg\u2026\u0022\r\nGER_la_amargura_del_fracaso:0 \u0022the bitterness of the faliure\u0022\r\nGER_la_amargura_del_fracaso_desc:0 \u0022Although we tried, the negotiations haven\u0027t gone as planned, so now we can only hope that the status quo is maintained and that there are no major changes.\u0022\r\nGER_unpactoconsatan:0 \u0022a pact with Satan??\u0022\r\nGER_unpactoconsatan_desc:0 \u0022The British Empire... is one of the largest and most magnificent empires that has ever existed; however, our struggle for global hegemony has always kept us in confrontational situations. Yet perhaps there is a chance that, for the first time in history, that will change; it\u0027s worth trying, even if it\u0027s just for a little while.\u0022\r\nGER_vestirse_de_oveja:0 \u0022dressing as a sheep\u0022\r\nGER_vestirse_de_oveja_desc:0 \u0022To the British, we\u0027re still those heartless, vengeful monsters. However, the reality is that while that\u0027s partly true, it doesn\u0027t mean that\u0027s all we are or that there aren\u0027t reasons to act this way. We just need the British to see it. Who knows how far we can go?\u0022\r\nGER_algo_para_lo_que_no_estamos_preparados:0 \u0022something we are not prepared for\u0022\r\nGER_algo_para_lo_que_no_estamos_preparados_desc:0 \u0022Our disastrous performance in Poland made it clear that our army is not prepared for a conflict of this kind. We will have to address this later, but for now, our only option is to survive.\u0022\r\nGER_movilizar_unidades_freikorps:0 \u0022movilizar unidades freikorps\u0022\r\nGER_movilizar_unidades_freikorps_desc:0 \u0022The Freikorps have historically been combat units that haven\u0027t been used in battles against large nations; however, this could be the exception to the rule. If we try using them for skirmishes, we might see them prove to be a significant asset.\u0022\r\nGER_problemas_inseperados:0 \u0022unexpected problems\u0022\r\nGER_problemas_inseperados_desc:0 \u0022In one of our skirmishes, several of our officers were captured, so we had to negotiate a halt to the skirmishes in order to get them back. Although the matter fortunately wasn\u0027t made public, it does speak to the poor state of our army for a conflict of that kind.\u0022\r\nGER_estonoestafuncionando:0 \u0022this is not working...\u0022\r\nGER_estonoestafuncionando_desc:0 \u0022Despite our efforts, things don\u0027t seem to be improving; on the contrary, they\u0027re getting worse every day. We\u0027ll have to change course if we want better results.\u0022\r\nGER_rise_of_the_reaction:0 \u0022Rise of the reaction\u0022\r\nGER_rise_of_the_reaction_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_victory_of_the_remormist:0 \u0022victory of the remormist\u0022\r\nGER_victory_of_the_remormist_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_the_national_momentum:0 \u0022the national momentum\u0022\r\nGER_the_national_momentum_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_begin_the_economic_counterstrike:0 \u0022begin the economic counter-strike\u0022\r\nGER_begin_the_economic_counterstrike_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_revive_the_imperial_army:0 \u0022revive the imperial army\u0022\r\nGER_revive_the_imperial_army_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_the_ludendorf_vision:0 \u0022the ludendorf vision\u0022\r\nGER_the_ludendorf_vision_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_stabbed_in_the_back:0 \u0022stabbed in the back\u0022\r\nGER_stabbed_in_the_back_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_thefreikorpsareuntouchable:0 \u0022\u0022The Freikorps are untouchable...\u0022\r\nGER_thefreikorpsareuntouchable_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_the_nation_does_not_negotiate:0 \u0022The nation does not negotiate\u0022\r\nGER_the_nation_does_not_negotiate_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_fix_the_political_situation:0 \u0022fix the political situation\u0022\r\nGER_fix_the_political_situation_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_order_must_prevail:0 \u0022Order Must Prevail\u0022\r\nGER_order_must_prevail_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_prohibit_public_demonstrations:0 \u0022prohibit public demonstrations\u0022\r\nGER_prohibit_public_demonstrations_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_force_Hugenberg_to_take_a_vacation:0 \u0022Force Hugenberg to take a \u0022vacation\u0022\u0022\r\nGER_force_Hugenberg_to_take_a_vacation_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_everythingwithinthestatenothingagainstthestate:0 \u0022Everything within the State, nothing against the State\u0022\r\nGER_everythingwithinthestatenothingagainstthestate_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_oath_to_the_supreme_commander:0 \u0022oath to the supreme commander\u0022\r\nGER_oath_to_the_supreme_commander_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_tamed_war_dogs:0 \u0022Tamed War Dogs\u0022\r\nGER_tamed_war_dogs_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_integrate_the_freikorps_into_the_state:0 \u0022Integrate the Freikorps into the State\u0022\r\nGER_integrate_the_freikorps_into_the_state_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_buttheyreform:0 \u0022...but they reform\u0022\u0022\r\nGER_buttheyreform_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_purging_of_unfair_elements:0 \u0022purging of unfair elements\u0022\r\nGER_purging_of_unfair_elements_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_keep_an_eye_on_the_reformers:0 \u0022keep an eye on the reformers\u0022\r\nGER_keep_an_eye_on_the_reformers_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_centralize_decision_making:0 \u0022Centralize Decision Making\u0022\r\nGER_centralize_decision_making_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_unifying_the_national_narrative:0 \u0022Unifying the National Narrative\u0022\r\nGER_unifying_the_national_narrative_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_identification_of_antinational_elements:0 \u0022Identification of Anti-national Elements\u0022\r\nGER_identification_of_antinational_elements_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_emergency_courts:0 \u0022Emergency Courts\u0022\r\nGER_emergency_courts_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_the_enemy_lives_among_us:0 \u0022The Enemy Lives Among Us\u0022\r\nGER_the_enemy_lives_among_us_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_the_nation_does_not_forget:0 \u0022The Nation Does Not Forget\u0022\r\nGER_the_nation_does_not_forget_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_everything_is_ready:0 \u0022everything is ready\u0022\r\nGER_everything_is_ready_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_focus_on_the_west:0 \u0022focus on the west\u0022\r\nGER_focus_on_the_west_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_schlieffen_once_again:0 \u0022Schlieffen once again\u0022\r\nGER_schlieffen_once_again_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_operational_planning_against_france:0 \u0022Operational Planning Against France\u0022\r\nGER_operational_planning_against_france_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_logistical_preparations_for_the_west:0 \u0022Logistical preparations for the west\u0022\r\nGER_logistical_preparations_for_the_west_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_justlikeintheolddays:0 \u0022Just like in the old days...\u0022\r\nGER_justlikeintheolddays_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_our_honor_recovered:0 \u0022our honor recovered\u0022\r\nGER_our_honor_recovered_desc:0 \u0022a\u0022\r\nGER_efforts_to_free_the_market:0 \u0022efforts to free the market\u0022\r\nGER_efforts_to_free_the_market_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_efforts_towards_autarky:0 \u0022efforts towards autarky\u0022\r\nGER_efforts_towards_autarky_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_alittleausteritywontgonahurt:0 \u0022A Little Austerity Won\u0027t Gona Hurt\u0022\r\nGER_alittleausteritywontgonahurt_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_to_win_the_favor_of_corporations:0 \u0022To Win The Favor Of Corporations\u0022\r\nGER_to_win_the_favor_of_corporations_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_managetheheavyindustry:0 \u0022\u0022Manage\u0022 The Heavy Industry\u0022\r\nGER_managetheheavyindustry_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_subordinate_the_economy_to_the_state:0 \u0022Subordinate the Economy to the State\u0022\r\nGER_subordinate_the_economy_to_the_state_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_continue_focusing_on_the_military_industry:0 \u0022Continue Focusing on the Military Industry\u0022\r\nGER_continue_focusing_on_the_military_industry_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_resource_selfsufficiency:0 \u0022Resource Self-Sufficiency\u0022\r\nGER_resource_selfsufficiency_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_raise_taxes_on_nonessential_businesses:0 \u0022Raise Taxes On Non-Essential Businesses\u0022\r\nGER_raise_taxes_on_nonessential_businesses_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_state_directorate_of_production:0 \u0022State Directorate of Production\u0022\r\nGER_state_directorate_of_production_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_make_deals_with_big_industrialists:0 \u0022Make Deals With Big Industrialists\u0022\r\nGER_make_deals_with_big_industrialists_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_towards_a_corporate_state:0 \u0022Towards A Corporate State\u0022\r\nGER_towards_a_corporate_state_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_demobilization_can_wait:0 \u0022Demobilization Can Wait\u0022\r\nGER_demobilization_can_wait_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_wewillfixtheeconomyeventually:0 \u0022We will fix the economy... Eventually...\u0022\r\nGER_wewillfixtheeconomyeventually_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_necessary_sacrifices:0 \u0022Necessary Sacrifices\u0022\r\nGER_necessary_sacrifices_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\nGER_towards_a_selfsufficient_germany:0 \u0022towards a self-sufficient Germany\u0022\r\nGER_towards_a_selfsufficient_germany_desc:0 \u0022.\u0022\r\n",
    "localisation/ideas_kaiser-wilhiem-ii_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\nkaiser_wilhiem_ii:0 \u0022Kaiser Wilhiem II\u0022\r\nkaiser_wilhiem_ii_desc:0 \u0022To say that Kaiser Wilhelm II is no longer what he once was would be an understatement. He not only led our country to ruin due to his incompetence and the breakdown in communication between the aristocracy and the common people, but it\u0027s also undeniable that he remains a symbol of both unity and stability, at least for the officers and a certain segment of our government. Ultimately, he\u0027s not going to save our government, but at least he\u0027s better than nothing. At the end of the day, he\u0027s well aware that he has no say in matters concerning the state.\u0022\r\novermobilized_industry:0 \u0022over-mobilized industry\u0022\r\novermobilized_industry_desc:0 \u0022For over a decade, the German economy has been focused on one thing, achieving revenge at any cost, regardless of the price. However, it doesn\u0027t take a genius to realize that this approach would have consequences. The economy has been under immense strain for years, resulting in what is, at best, profoundly mediocre performance. While some voices are suggesting we should try to open up and end the protests, there are still people in the government who flatly refuse to do so.\u0022\r\nthe_freikorps_question:0 \u0022the Freikorps question\u0022\r\nthe_freikorps_question_desc:0 \u0022The issue of the Freikorps has been a topic of debate ever since we managed to stage the coup back in 1920. It\u0027s undeniable that the Freikorps were composed of people who cherish their country and its traditional values, so we can\u0027t simply forget them. However, maintaining the Freikorps has proven to have long-term problems. Their inherently \u0022free\u0022 nature has given them far more freedom to do as they please, and consequently, abuses of power have been commonplace over the past decade. Not to mention that their ability to guarantee peace has been called into question since the 1929 crash, so it\u0027s clear that reform or even complete dissolution is needed, although, of course, this is something no one in the government dares to do.\u0022\r\nthe_stillfresh_memory_of_the_great_war:0 \u0022the still-fresh memory of the great war\u0022\r\nthe_stillfresh_memory_of_the_great_war_desc:0 \u0022Although the Great War has ended, its memory remains with both the population and the army. The memories of the trenches still terrify some soldiers, so it\u0027s not surprising that many people are no longer so enthusiastic about going to the front. However, on the other hand, this conflict has given us true veteran killing machines that will be a perfect fit.\u0022\r\nalmost_no_international_support:0 \u0022almost no international support\u0022\r\nalmost_no_international_support_desc:0 \u0022It is no surprise that almost ignoring the Treaty of Versailles would have long-term consequences. The United States and its allies wanted a liberal state that would bow its head and accept that they were the champions of the new century. Instead, they found themselves with a state as militaristic as it was vengeful. Given this scenario, it is no wonder that our position on the world stage is dire.\u0022\r\nmemoirs_of_1929:0 \u0022Memoirs of 1929\u0022\r\nmemoirs_of_1929_desc:0 \u0022The 1929 crisis was almost the final nail in the coffin of our government. It demonstrated that we could not simply continue with our government in the long term and revealed its weakness. Although we managed to stop the protests, it came at a tremendous cost, largely losing the support of those who might even have sympathized with us. In response, different proposals have been put forward. The reformist wing, led by Hugenberg, says it was a mistake, while figures like Ludendorff refuse to admit it, uttering his famous phrase, \u0022I would do it again and a thousand times if necessary.\u0022 In any case, whichever faction inherits the Reich will not be able to ignore this problem.\u0022\r\n",
    "localisation/localisation_for_superevents_l_english.yml": "l_english:\r\n \r\n  SUPER_EVENT_T:0 \u0022The Second Great War\u0022\r\n  SUPER_EVENT_D:0 \u0022I reject Christianity because it is Jewish, because it is international, and because, in cowardly fashion, it preaches Peace on Earth. -Erich Ludendorff\u0022\r\n  SUPER_EVENT_A:0 \u0022Freikorps Voran!!\u0022",
    "localisation/parties_l_english.yml": "l_english:\n communism:0 \u0022Communist\u0022\n communism_noun:0 \u0022Communism\u0022\n democratic:0 \u0022Democratic\u0022\n democratic_noun:0 \u0022Democracy\u0022\n fascism:0 \u0022Fascist\u0022\n fascism_noun:0 \u0022Fascism\u0022\n fascism_desc:0 \u0022Totalitarian Regime\u0022\n communism_desc:0 \u0022Totalitarian Regime\u0022\n democratic_desc:0 \u0022Democratic Regime\u0022\n conservatism:0 \u0022Conservatism\u0022\n conservatism_desc:0 \u0022Considering rapid changes to society to be potentially harmful, conservatism espouses tradition and moderate reforms, sometimes advocating a return to old moral values.\u0022\n liberalism:0 \u0022Liberalism\u0022\n liberalism_desc:0 \u0022With a long philosophical tradition of valuing personal liberty, liberalism views safeguarding these rights as the primary function of the state.\u0022\n socialism:0 \u0022Socialism\u0022\n socialism_desc:0 \u0022Striving for equality and a socialist state by reformist means, democratic socialism aims to abolish or mitigate the effects of capitalism with public mandate.\u0022\n marxism:0 \u0022Marxism\u0022\n marxism_desc:0 \u0022Encompassing a broad spectrum of economic and historical views, Marxist politics seek to apply the theories of Karl Marx to political practice. Class struggle and the need for transition to a society based on common ownership of the means of production characterize these ideologies.\u0022\n leninism:0 \u0022Leninism\u0022\n leninism_desc:0 \u0022A political ideology based in Marxist thought, Leninism seeks to establish a socialist state by a vanguard party leading a revolution overthrowing capitalist society. Once in power, the party rules through a system whereby policies are open for internal debate until a decision has been made.\u0022\n stalinism:0 \u0022Stalinism\u0022\n stalinism_desc:1 \u0022Identifying as a form of government applying and developing Marxist-Leninist policies, Stalinism emphasizes rapid industrialization and collectivization as well as the need for a strong, authoritative socialist state to purge any counter-revolutionary elements.\u0022\n anti_revisionism:0 \u0022Anti-Revisionism\u0022\n anti_revisionism_desc:0 \u0022A reaction to the many ideologies claiming to be successors to Marxism, Anti-Revisionism advocates retaining key elements of original revolutionary theory. Mainly opposing incorporation of capitalist economic elements into socialist states, the ideology is defined as much by what it isn\u0027t as what it is.\u0022\n anarchist_communism:0 \u0022Anarchist Communism\u0022\n anarchist_communism_desc:0 \u0022An ideology embracing the idea of communism as a stateless society, Anarchist Communism eschews the idea of a transitionary socialist state and favors a society based on voluntary associations and mutual aid.\u0022\n nazism:0 \u0022Nazism\u0022\n nazism_desc:0 \u0022Rooted in extreme nationalism, National Socialism is driven by ideas of Germanic supremacy. It promotes aggressive expansionism and a totalitarian state where the people are united under a leader with absolute power, the F\u00FChrer.\u0022\n gen_nazism:0 \u0022Nazism\u0022\n gen_nazism_desc:0 \u0022Rooted in extreme nationalism, National Socialism is driven by ideas of racial supremacy. It promotes aggressive expansionism and a totalitarian state where the people are united under a leader with absolute power.\u0022\n fascism_ideology:0 \u0022Fascism\u0022\n fascism_ideology_desc:0 \u0022Encompassing a variety of ultra-nationalist movements, fascism typically venerates devotion to the state and uniting the people under a strong leader.\u0022\n falangism:0 \u0022Falangism\u0022\n falangism_desc:0 \u0022An authoritarian ideology with traits of fascism and conservatism, Falangism values national and Catholic identity.\u0022\n rexism:0 \u0022Rexism\u0022\n rexism_desc:0 \u0022Strongly opposed to both liberal and communist ideals, Rexism is a staunchly conservative nationalist movement who advocate a corporatist economic policy. Employing increasingly populist and authoritarian rhetoric, their ideals are shifting closer to other fascist movements.\u0022\n neutrality:0 \u0022Non-Aligned\u0022\n neutrality_noun:0 \u0022Non-Aligned\u0022\n neutrality_desc:0 \u0022Authoritarian Regime\u0022\n orthodox_reactionism:0 \u0022orthodox reactionism\u0022\n orthodox_reactionism_desc:0 \u0022The past was always better is a phrase that easily describes orthodox reactionaries. Anchored directly to the past, these individuals tend to see the existence of elites and the status quo as intrinsic to human nature. However, unlike traditional conservatives, they believe the answer to all of society\u0027s problems is a return to a bygone era, \u0022far removed from the chaos and degeneration of the present.\u0022 Although they often wield the most control within governments and radical right-wing movements, their lack of initiative regarding almost any change makes people doubt their long-term reliability, particularly that of their allies, the \u0022dissident reactionaries.\u0022 Furthermore, unlike the latter, they don\u0027t tend to have an exaggerated cult of personality due to their generally \u0022sensible\u0022 nature. However, with the rapid changes the world is undergoing, it\u0027s quite difficult to envision a world where their desires can be fulfilled. In any case, they are still the ones who have led German politics, and until something very disruptive happens, it is difficult to think of an alternative.\u0022\n disident_reactionism:0 \u0022disident reactionism\u0022\n disident_reactionism_desc:0 \u0022Unlike their orthodox counterparts, dissident reactionaries, while they appreciate the past and recognize the importance of its preservation, do not see a return to it as their primary objective. On the contrary, they seek to create something new through it. While this hasn\u0027t led them to be viewed as a variant of fascism, the reality is that they have marked differences. For example, while they may develop personality cults and be authoritarian, this doesn\u0027t reach the levels of Soviet or Italian totalitarianism. Furthermore, dissident reactionaries don\u0027t necessarily present themselves as revolutionaries, but rather as \u0022knights of reaction\u0022 due to a much more fervent preservation of elites than fascists. However, they share the orthodox view that the modern world has been plagued by degeneration and chaos, and that it can only be restored with an iron fist. Still, their more dynamic nature makes them more appealing to the masses, especially the youth, who see in them a way to channel their discontent with the current state of affairs. Whether they will be able to achieve their goals in the face of rapid societal changes remains to be seen, but they are undoubtedly a force to be reckoned with in the political landscape.\u0022\n despotism:0 \u0022Despotic\u0022\n despotism_desc:0 \u0022Despotism is a form of government in which a single person rules with absolute power.\u0022\n oligarchism:0 \u0022Oligarchic\u0022\n oligarchism_desc:0 \u0022Oligarchy is a form of government in which a group of people rule with absolute power.\u0022\n moderatism:1 \u0022Moderatism\u0022\n moderatism_desc:1 \u0022Moderatism is a form of government which avoids the extremes of left and right by taking a moderate position or course of action.\u0022\n centrism:1 \u0022Centrism\u0022\n centrism_desc:1 \u0022Centrism is a form of government which wants to achieve common sense solutions that appropriately address current and future needs, that support the public trust and serve the common good with consideration of risk and capacity in context of these needs.\u0022\n anarchism:0 \u0022Anarchism\u0022\n anarchism_desc:0 \u0022Anarchism is the rejection of authority itself, promoting the division of society into self-managing and self-governing collectives instead of a singular, centralized state.\u0022\n GER_fascism_part