    {
      "Id": "events_for_initial.1",
      "Type": "country_event",
      "Title": "events_for_initial.1.t",
      "Description": "L\u00FCttwitz looked with disdain at the economic report for the past year. It was as mediocre as it had always been since he\u0027d taken command back in 1922. However, things seemed to be changing in recent months. After all, the conflict with Poland had finally allowed him to mobilize and make good use of our already depleted war economy, for something practical and immediate. Although he knew this was only temporary, it was also something that could offer a glimmer of hope in the abyss that had been in the country for years. \\n\\nHowever, a debate remained regarding this reactivation of the economy, since the military used it as justification for mobilizing more people to the battlefield, while others spoke of taking advantage of the situation to gradually rebuild civilian industry, keeping people employed in the factories. It was a difficult decision for him. A few years ago, he wouldn\u0027t have hesitated to simply send people to war to retake the imperial possessions. However, political reality seems to have changed him more than he initially expected, so after thinking about it for a while he said to himself",
      "Picture": "qu_hacer_con_la_poblacin-487",
      "PictureSource": "",
      "TriggeredOnly": false,
      "FireOnlyOnce": true,
      "Hidden": false,
      "Major": false,
      "Trigger": "has_completed_focus = GER_quehacerconlapoblacion",
      "MeanTimeToHappen": "days = 1",
      "Immediate": "",
      "After": "",
      "Options": [
        {
          "Name": "wee need more soldiers",
          "Trigger": "",
          "AiChance": "",
          "Effect": "create_unit = {\r\n    division = \u0022name = \\\u0022[Low_freikorps]\\\u0022 division_template = \\\u0022[Low_Freikorps_units]\\\u0022 start_experience_factor = [0;1] start_equipment_factor = [0;1]\u0022\r\n    owner = [Ger]\r\n}\r\noption = {\r\n    name = events_for_initial.1.b\r\n    industrial_capacity_factor = 0.10\r\n}\r\nhidden_effect = {\r\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Id": "events_for_initial.2",
      "Type": "country_event",
      "Title": "a litle aproche",
      "Description": "King Edward paused for a moment, gazing at a photograph of the former king George V, and a thought crossed his mind, did he really have to do this? He could very well be enjoying a quiet afternoon with his wife or simply indulging in his many and varied luxuries. Yet here he was, dealing with a political crisis that, honestly, he did not care about. \\n(Wolfgang Kapp enters the room)\\n-(Edward thought for a moment before speaking)\\n\u0022Very well, thank you for asking, and thank you for coming to the meeting,\u201D Edward replied.\\n\u0022I would like to get straight to the point and address directly the issues concerning the Polish crisis and its implications.\u0022-\\n(Edward did not quite know how to respond; his life had not prepared him for decisions of this kind, and besides, he honestly did not care much about the topic.)\\n\u0022\u201CUh\u2026 yes, yes, about that matter\u2026\u201D\u0022-\u201CI remind you that our nation is fully aware of how this may appear, and we assure you that the sole objective of our nation is the restoration and respect of our national pride\u2014\u201D (Edward interrupted him,) \u201CYes, yes, yes, I know, but you know, I also wanted to take the opportunity to talk about other things, you know?\u201D (Kapp looked at him, puzzled.) \u201CWhat exactly do you mean, Mr. Edward?\u201D \u201CWell, you see, I would like to know more about this \u2018German food.\u2019 I\u2019ve heard wonders about it.\u201D Kapp stared at Edward in complete disbelief. Was this the man who would soon be monarch? After some time processing this, an idea came to mind.      \\n\\n\u201COf course, Mr. Edward. We could even offer you our finest German chefs, in exchange, of course, for a little positive feedback from us.\u201D\\nEdward simply smiled.",
      "Picture": "un_pequeo_acercamiento-844",
      "PictureSource": "",
      "TriggeredOnly": false,
      "FireOnlyOnce": true,
      "Hidden": false,
      "Major": false,
      "Trigger": "has_completed_focus = GER_la_lucha_en_la_mesa",
      "MeanTimeToHappen": "days = 1",
      "Immediate": "",
      "After": "",
      "Options": [
        {
          "Name": "seems like we have a deal",
          "Trigger": "",
          "AiChance": "",
          "Effect": "hidden_effect = {\r\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Id": "events_for_initial.5",
      "Type": "country_event",
      "Title": "domesticated war dogs",
      "Description": "The Freikorps, originally created by the SPD government back in 1919, have been one of the most influential paramilitary groups of the century. Comparisons to the Soviets and the poor Keresky government are common. One might think that after Kampp\u0027s coup, the Freikorps would simply be dissolved, but time would prove otherwise. They proved to be a loophole in the Treaty of Versailles, and even when it was revised in 1921, the terms limiting the Freikorps proved to be very lax, ultimately leading to their integration into German politics.\\n\\n However, there\u0027s something that\u0027s rarely mentioned about them, something obvious to anyone who works in areas like the military:the Freikorps were mostly made up of traumatized veterans of the First World War, frustrated and angry people who, in what seemed like the end of everything they knew, banded together to save what little remained... of a world that seemed to have abandoned them. It\u0027s to be expected that, given this context, they wouldn\u0027t be so loyal to their aristocratic officers or their Supreme Commander.\\n\\n This is why there has been a recent power struggle between the regular army and the Freikorps, which, for the moment, has been contained. However, under the increasingly unified leadership of Ernst R\u00F6hm and his increasingly populist rhetoric, he seems to be attracting more and more Freikorps, both young and old. With the arrival of our new administration, it will be quite clear that the Freikorps will not be easy to appease.",
      "Picture": "freikorps_history",
      "PictureSource": "",
      "TriggeredOnly": false,
      "FireOnlyOnce": true,
      "Hidden": false,
      "Major": false,
      "Trigger": "has_completed_focus = GER_rise_of_the_reaction",
      "MeanTimeToHappen": "days = 1",
      "Immediate": "",
      "After": "",
      "Options": [
        {
          "Name": "ein, volk ein, kaiser...",
          "Trigger": "",
          "AiChance": "",
          "Effect": "hidden_effect = {\r\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Id": "historia_del_estado_aleman.1",
      "Type": "country_event",
      "Title": "el estado aleman",
      "Description": "El estado aleman es una entidad que es declarada en 1920 tras el golpe de estado hecho por wolf kapp y las unidades paramilitares \u201Cfreikorps\u201D\\n",
      "Picture": "el_estado_aleman-487",
      "PictureSource": "",
      "TriggeredOnly": false,
      "FireOnlyOnce": true,
      "Hidden": false,
      "Major": false,
      "Trigger": "",
      "MeanTimeToHappen": "days = 1",
      "Immediate": "",
      "After": "",
      "Options": [
        {
          "Name": "si honestamente no me interesa el lore",
          "Trigger": "",
          "AiChance": "factor = 1",
          "Effect": "hidden_effect = {\r\n}"
        },
        {
          "Name": "y como paso ese golpe de estado?",
          "Trigger": "",
          "AiChance": "factor = 1",
          "Effect": "country_event = {\r\n    id = historia_del_estado_aleman.2\r\n    days = 0\r\n    random = 50\r\n    random_days = 10\r\n}\r\nhidden_effect = {\r\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Id": "historia_del_estado_aleman.2",
      "Type": "country_event",
      "Title": "EL GOLPE DE ESTADO",
      "Description": "la conspiraci\u00F3n inicia con la sensaci\u00F3n de escepticismo de la derecha hacia la rep\u00FAblica socialdem\u00F3crata, habido pasado por un intento de revoluci\u00F3n en alemania por los llamados \u201Cespartaquistas\u201D, siendo un intento de instaurar comunismo en la joven rep\u00FAblica, es as\u00ED que el gobierno crea las unidades paramilitares conocidas como \u201Cfreikorps\u201D hechas de veteranos de la primera guerra mundial y por j\u00F3venes anti-comunistas, estas unidades aplastaron la revuelta y matar\u00EDan a los l\u00EDderes rosa luxemburgo y \u2026. Es as\u00ED como estas unidades cobran un peso extremadamente importante para m\u00E1s tarde.\\n\\npara 1920 la derecha alemana todav\u00EDa no se sent\u00EDa ni quer\u00EDa estar c\u00F3modo con la idea de una democracia liberal sin mencionar claro el tratado de versalles que proponia cosas como reducir la fuerza del ej\u00E9rcito a 100.000 cosa que claro a la derecha molesto demasiado, es por esto que organizaron un golpe de estado que no entrar\u00EDa en vigor hasta en el 29 de febrero de 1920, esto debido a que por las estipulaciones del tratado de versalles, el ej\u00E9rcito se vio obligado a disolver una brigada de la marina y un cuerpo de voluntarios, debido a esto El 10 de marzo de 1920, el general Walther von L\u00FCttwitz exigi\u00F3 del presidente Friedrich Ebert y del ministro de Defensa Gustav Noske que se dejar\u00E1 de reducir las tropas, que se disolviese el parlamento y que se eligiese el presidente directamente por el pueblo. Ebert y Noske rechazaron estas exigencias y le dieron vacaciones forzosas a von L\u00FCttwitz. Entonces von L\u00FCttwitz decidi\u00F3 llevar a cabo un golpe de Estado.\\n\\nel 13 de marzo L\u00FCttwitz decidi\u00F3 partir con una brigada a berl\u00EDn, el ej\u00E9rcito regular se neg\u00F3 a combatir a los golpistas y como resultado Friedrich Ebert y Gustav se vieron forzados a huir, de manera que Wolfgang Kapp se nombr\u00F3 a s\u00ED mismo canciller y a von L\u00FCttwitz ministro de Defensa y comandante en jefe del ej\u00E9rcito es as\u00ED como los funcionarios de berl\u00EDn se negaron a acatar sus \u00F3rdenes y llamaron a un paro general. Sin embargo debido a los comunistas todavia resentidos por los asesinatos de Rosa Luxemburgo llamaron a no hacer el paro.\\n\\nfue de esta manera que a pesar de que el paro fue en cierta parte efectivo los llamados del partido comunista a no hacer paros dificulto mucho su efectividad. De manera que con el pasar de los dias y dias, los paros fueran poco a poco perdiendo fuerza hasta que finalmente Wolfgang Kapp pudo finalmente cimentar su control sobre berl\u00EDn y cuando el partido comunista se dio cuenta de su error fue demasiado tarde. r\u00E1pidamente Wolfgang mando a banear al partido comunista y matar a todos los de este, la mayor\u00EDa terminaria huyendo a hungria y despu\u00E9s rusia y los que no terminaron masacrados por las unidades freikorps\\n",
      "Picture": "el_golpe_de_estado-1",
      "PictureSource": "",
      "TriggeredOnly": true,
      "FireOnlyOnce": true,
      "Hidden": false,
      "Major": false,
      "Trigger": "",
      "MeanTimeToHappen": "",
      "Immediate": "",
      "After": "",
      "Options": [
        {
          "Name": "interesante",
          "Trigger": "",
          "AiChance": "factor = 1",
          "Effect": "country_event = {\r\n    id = historia_del_estado_aleman.3\r\n    days = 0\r\n    random = 50\r\n    random_days = 10\r\n}\r\nhidden_effect = {\r\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Id": "historia_del_estado_aleman.3",
      "Type": "country_event",
      "Title": "intento de golpe de estado y normalizacion",
      "Description": " a pesar de que el gobierno de wolfgang se mantuvo relativamente estable en los siguientes a\u00F1os las cosas tomarian un giro drastico en 1922 con la muerte de kamppf, esto no seria desaprovechado por ludendorf y el ala conservadora que se negaba a acpetar el gobierno de continuidad de luttwitz, de manera que en la primavera de 1923, ludendorf y su sequito intentarian hacer un contra-golpe de estado, sin embargo el resultado quedo inconcluso, ya que durante los primeros dias ludendorf no fue capas de neutralizar a los lideres del ruling goverment por lo que seguiria en esos dias seria un caos absoluto, obreros tomando las calles, peleas entre las propias freikops y casi nula comunicacion, por lo que al ver lo que estaba pasando, ludendorf decidio abandonar el golpe y tratar de evitar una guerra civil o la llegada de ideas comunistas al poder, sin embargo los metodos para socabar las protestas que ludendorf y sus unidades hicieron fueron tan extremas que se le conoce como \u00BF\u0022la masacre hamburgo\u0022 donde se dio ordenes de disparar a matar a cualquiera que protestara en las calles, ludendorf no solo no se disculpo nunca sino que dijo su famosa frase \u0022lo haria una y mil veces mas de ser necesario\u0022. Apesar de el golpe de estado haber fracasado, esto no significo la muerte del ala de linea dura, debido al respeto y aprecio que tenian los oficiales a ludendorf, luttwitz sabia que apresar o siquiera obligar al retiro a ludendorf seria un movimiento demaciado arriesgado asique se centro principalmente en contener su posible influencia politica. Aunque esto sin duda fue algo que el gobierno no deseaba tuvo tambien su lado positivo, con los radicales ya agotados politicamente, luttwitz decide aprovechar la oportunidad para hacer un tratado economico con la urss que le permitiria a alemania no solo pagar sus deudas de guerra y sacarla de la crisis sino que ademas romper su aislamiento tanto economico como diplomatico, siendo sin duda un movimiento que le daria un respiro enorme al todavia joven estado aleman",
      "Picture": "el_post_golpe-1",
      "PictureSource": "",
      "TriggeredOnly": true,
      "FireOnlyOnce": true,
      "Hidden": false,
      "Major": false,
      "Trigger": "",
